PICS 0
BACnet Protocol Implementation Conformance Statement
Vendor Name: "Chipkin Automation Systems"
Product Name: "CAS BACnet Stack Example - B-EM"
Product Model Number: "CAS BACnet Stack Example - B-EM"
Product Description: "A read-only BACnet/IP monitor for an elevator installation, built on the CAS BACnet Stack. It presents the series' three base sensor objects plus an Elevator Group / Lift / Escalator object family; the Lift follows a simulated lift car as it moves floor to floor. It answers ReadProperty and ReadPropertyMultiple, supports SubscribeCOV and SubscribeCOVPropertyMultiple (including the car's Car_Position, Car_Moving_Direction and Car_Door_Status), generates intrinsic event notifications (CHANGE_OF_STATE on the Lift's Passenger_Alarm, FAULT_LISTED on its Fault_Signals), accepts AcknowledgeAlarm, answers GetEventInformation, and handles DeviceCommunicationControl. It accepts WriteProperty only for Notification Class 1's Recipient_List (commissioning the alarm recipients), and no WritePropertyMultiple, Schedule, ReinitializeDevice or TimeSynchronization. It is a tutorial for implementers of the B-EM profile."

BACnet Standardized Device Profiles Supported:
{
B-EM - BACnet Elevator Monitor
}

BIBBs Supported:
{
DS-RP-B
DS-RPM-B
DS-COV-B
DS-COVM-B
AE-N-I-B
AE-ACK-B
AE-INFO-B
DM-DDB-B
DM-DOB-B
DM-DCC-B
}

BACnet Standard Application Services Supported:
{
AcknowledgeAlarm Execute
ConfirmedCOVNotification Initiate
ConfirmedEventNotification Initiate
SubscribeCOV Execute
ReadProperty Execute
ReadPropertyMultiple Execute
WriteProperty Execute
DeviceCommunicationControl Execute
IAm Initiate
IHave Initiate
UnconfirmedCOVNotification Initiate
UnconfirmedEventNotification Initiate
WhoHas Execute
WhoIs Execute
GetEventInformation Execute
SubscribeCOVPropertyMultiple Execute
ConfirmedCOVNotificationMultiple Initiate
UnconfirmedCOVNotificationMultiple Initiate
}

